    {
      "id": "claim_39b6302cfd9543cb870927ffbdc61cee",
      "statement": "The CI gate is go vet ./... && go test ./... (never hits the network) plus a clean gofmt -l .; unit/integration tests never touch the network (live paths env-gated via YOLO_LLM=fake) and the live e2e is user-run, never CI; just e2e-live (scripts/e2e-live.sh) builds the binary, boots yolo serve from a scratch project pinned to the real kido endpoint, and drives health check -> create a yolo-agent session -> send 'list files in /tmp' (asserts a completed tool call + a non-empty text reply) -> abort tests (idle -> aborted:false, busy -> aborted:true) -> SIGTERM -> graceful exit 0, requiring KIDO_API_KEY.",
